//!
//! # `gororoba_gpu_readback` Extraction Scope
//!
//! ## Purpose
//!
//! This scope defines what should and should not move into a lightweight
//! `gororoba_gpu_readback` crate.
//!
//! The crate is meant to standardize host-visible staging and readback contracts
//! across CUDA and Vulkan workloads without importing solver ownership, Vulkan
//! command submission policy, or domain-specific frame semantics.
//!
//! ## Why Extract It
//!
//! The repo already has more than one readback pattern:
//!
//! - CUDA solver density and velocity host copies in `lbm_3d_cuda`
//! - OptiX orchestrator host-visible particle buffers
//! - Vulkan render/image readback in `lbm_vulkan`
//!
//! Today those paths are duplicated enough to justify a small contract crate, but
//! not a massive backend runtime abstraction.
//!
//! ## Candidate Public Surface
//!
//! ### Core descriptors
//!
//! - `ReadbackBufferShape`
//! - width, height, depth, element count
//! - `ReadbackElementType`
//! - `U8`, `U16`, `U32`, `F16`, `BF16`, `F32`, `F64`
//! - `ReadbackLayout`
//! - `Packed`
//! - `Soa`
//! - `Aos`
//! - `ImageRgba8`
//! - `ReadbackResidency`
//! - `PinnedHost`
//! - `MappedHost`
//! - `UnifiedManaged`
//! - `RendererOwned`
//!
//! ### Transfer contracts
//!
//! - `ReadbackDescriptor`
//! - shape
//! - element type
//! - layout
//! - byte length
//! - residency
//! - backend name
//! - `ReadbackRange`
//! - byte offset
//! - byte length
//! - optional logical subregion
//! - `ReadbackReport`
//! - transfer bytes
//! - elapsed time
//! - achieved GiB/s if known
//!
//! ### Traits
//!
//! - `HostReadableBuffer`
//! - metadata for a host-readable staging surface
//! - `ReadbackPlanner`
//! - choose full copy vs subrange copy vs tiled copy
//!
//! ## Good Extraction Candidates
//!
//! ### From `lbm_3d_cuda`
//!
//! - pinned host staging descriptors around `readback_rho_pinned()`
//! - host-side metadata for density/velocity readback ranges
//! - generic reporting for readback size and timing
//!
//! ### From `lbm_vulkan`
//!
//! - image/buffer readback descriptor vocabulary
//! - host-visible staging metadata
//! - generic copy-plan reporting
//!
//! ### From viewer-side code
//!
//! - frontend-visible distinction between direct host frames and copied frames
//!
//! ## Must Stay Local
//!
//! ### CUDA-local
//!
//! - kernel launch ownership
//! - stream synchronization policy
//! - sparse-solver memory-mode decisions
//! - solver-specific `sync_to_host()` and field unpacking semantics
//!
//! ### Vulkan-local
//!
//! - command-buffer recording
//! - queue submission
//! - layout transitions
//! - allocator ownership
//! - render-engine-specific image formats and barriers
//!
//! ### Solver / viewer local
//!
//! - interpretation of the copied bytes as density, velocity, entropy, or tracer
//! semantics
//!
//! ## Extraction Order
//!
//! 1. Introduce descriptor-only types first.
//! 2. Move shared reporting utilities next.
//! 3. Only then move tiny helper functions that do not drag backend runtimes into
//! >  the new crate.
//! 4. Leave backend execution and synchronization code in the owning crate.
//!
//! ## Success Criteria
//!
//! This extraction is worth doing only if it yields:
//!
//! - one shared vocabulary for host-staging/readback metadata
//! - no new dependency from lightweight crates onto CUDA or Vulkan runtime crates
//! - less duplication in viewer and profiling/report code
//!
//! If those conditions are not met, keep the helpers local.
//!
